From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Berg <fedora@slipsprogrammor.no>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 08:46:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Bind the bare arrow and page keys to mpv's seek steps

Seeking was only reachable through Ctrl+Left/Right, so the bare arrow keys
did nothing at all while a video played. Bind them the way mpv does by
default: 10 seconds on Left/Right, a minute on Up/Down, ten minutes on
Page_Up/Page_Down. Playback speed, which had Page_Up/Page_Down, moves to
Ctrl+Page_Up/Ctrl+Page_Down; Ctrl+Left/Right and the volume and speed
actions all keep working as before.

This adds a "seek" action taking a signed number of seconds, which is what
the FIXME next to drag-seek-forward asked for: the accelerators bind
detailed action names ("app.seek(-60)"), so a single action covers every
step size instead of one action per offset. The parameter is int64 because
that is what g_variant_parse() infers for a bare integer.

The shortcuts window is updated to match.
---
 data/net.base_art.Glide.ui | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 src/main.rs                | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/ui_context.rs          | 12 ++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 65 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

